-- Q11526: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under SFAC No. 8 (QC7-QC10) and ASC 275, relevance has two components: predictive value and confirmatory value. Information has confirmatory value when it provides feedback about prior evaluations. The actual $310,000 in warranty claims confirms or corrects investors'' prior assessment of the $250,000 estimate, fulfilling the confirmatory role.
Wrong (B): While the data may also help forecast future claims, the question specifically asks about evaluating a prior estimate''s accuracy, which is confirmatory rather than predictive value.
Wrong (C): Faithful representation is a separate fundamental characteristic concerning completeness, neutrality, and freedom from error, not a component of relevance.
Wrong (D): Timeliness is an enhancing characteristic about information being available early enough to influence decisions, not about validating prior estimates.$EXPL$
