-- Q11527: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 450-20-50, reasonably possible loss contingencies must be disclosed in the notes. ASC 450-20-50-4 permits omission of the specific loss estimate if disclosure would be prejudicial to the entity''s legal position, but the nature of the contingency must still be described.
Wrong (A): Disclosure is required for reasonably possible contingencies under the full disclosure principle; only recognition (accrual) requires the loss to be probable.
Wrong (B): Recognition of a liability requires both probable loss and a reasonably estimable amount; a reasonably possible loss does not meet the recognition threshold.
Wrong (C): The entity cannot omit all references to the lawsuit; the nature of the contingency must be disclosed even when the dollar estimate is omitted.$EXPL$
