-- Q11528: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under SFAC No. 8 (Chapter 4), a liability is a present obligation to transfer economic benefits arising from past transactions or events. Glacier''s receipt of $180,000 creates an obligation to perform consulting services, recognized as unearned revenue (a liability) under ASC 606.
Wrong (A): Revenue is recognized only when performance obligations are satisfied, not merely upon receipt of cash. The advance represents an unfulfilled obligation.
Wrong (C): Equity is the residual interest in assets after deducting liabilities. An advance payment increases both assets (cash) and liabilities (unearned revenue), not equity.
Wrong (D): A contingent liability depends on the outcome of an uncertain future event. Glacier''s obligation is certain and unconditional, not contingent.$EXPL$
