-- Q11529: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under SFAC No. 8 (QC19-QC34) and ASC 105-10-05, timeliness and verifiability are both enhancing qualitative characteristics. Timeliness means providing information early enough to influence decisions, while verifiability means independent observers can reach consensus. The framework requires balancing both to maximize decision-usefulness.
Wrong (A): Relevance and faithful representation are the two fundamental characteristics, not enhancing ones. This scenario involves enhancing characteristics (timeliness vs. verifiability), and no single characteristic always takes absolute priority.
Wrong (B): Comparability and consistency relate to cross-entity and cross-period comparisons, which are not at issue in this release-timing decision.
Wrong (D): Understandability and completeness are not the characteristics in tension here. The conflict is between releasing information quickly versus ensuring it is independently verifiable.$EXPL$
