-- Q11539: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 105-10-05-3, FASB Concepts Statements (such as SFAC No. 8) are explicitly identified as nonauthoritative. They provide the conceptual foundation for developing accounting standards but do not themselves establish GAAP requirements. The sole authoritative source for nongovernmental entities is the FASB ASC.
Wrong (A): Concepts Statements are not authoritative at all, let alone the most authoritative source. The FASB ASC is the single authoritative source of nongovernmental U.S. GAAP.
Wrong (C): Concepts Statements are nonauthoritative for all entities, not just governmental ones. Governmental entities follow GASB standards, not FASB Concepts Statements.
