-- Q11544: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under SFAC No. 8 (Chapter 4) and ASC 505-10-S99, equity is defined as the residual interest in the assets of an entity that remains after deducting its liabilities. Equity is derived from the accounting equation: Assets = Liabilities + Equity. It is not independently measured.
Wrong (B): Market capitalization represents the stock market''s valuation of outstanding shares, not the conceptual framework''s definition of equity. Book equity and market value differ.
Wrong (C): Cash available for distribution is a liquidity measure, not the definition of equity. Equity includes all net assets, not just distributable cash.
Wrong (D): Historical cost of contributed assets does not capture the full scope of equity, which also includes retained earnings, accumulated OCI, and other components beyond original contributions.$EXPL$
