  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under SFAC No. 8 (QC12-QC16), faithful representation requires three attributes: completeness, neutrality, and freedom from error. Completeness means including all information necessary for users to understand reported transactions. Omitting the related-party disclosure under ASC 850 means the statements lack completeness.
Wrong (A): Freedom from error is only one of three attributes of faithful representation. Accurate dollar amounts alone do not satisfy completeness or neutrality requirements.
Wrong (C): Related-party disclosures under ASC 850 are required disclosures, not optional supplements. Omitting them impairs the completeness component of faithful representation.
Wrong (D): Timeliness is an enhancing characteristic about when information is available. The omission of a required disclosure violates completeness under faithful representation, not timeliness.$EXPL$
