  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 105, Accounting Standards Updates are the mechanism by which the FASB amends the codification. ASUs add new guidance, modify existing requirements, or remove obsolete provisions within the ASC. Once applied, the updated ASC content becomes authoritative.
Wrong (B): ASUs do not replace the ASC; they update it. The FASB ASC remains the sole authoritative source of nongovernmental U.S. GAAP after each ASU is incorporated.
Wrong (C): ASUs are not nonauthoritative interpretive guidance. They are the formal vehicle for changing authoritative codification content.
Wrong (D): ASUs do not codify SEC rules. SEC guidance is separately maintained and incorporated into the ASC through distinct SEC sections, not through ASUs.$EXPL$
