-- Q11580: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 230-10-50-3, noncash investing and financing activities must be disclosed in a supplemental schedule, not in the body of the statement of cash flows. The debt-to-equity conversion involves no cash exchange and therefore does not appear in any of the three activity categories.
Wrong (A): Although both bonds and equity are financing items, the transaction involves no cash flows. Noncash transactions cannot appear in the operating, investing, or financing sections.
Wrong (B): The conversion does not involve investing activities. No long-lived assets are acquired or disposed of, and no cash changes hands.
Wrong (D): Operating activities involve revenue and expense-related cash flows. A bond-to-equity conversion has no connection to operations and involves no cash.$EXPL$
