-- Q11585: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 505-30, treasury stock is reported as a contra equity item, reducing total stockholders'' equity on the balance sheet. Whether recorded under the cost method or par value method, treasury stock decreases equity and is not an asset.
Wrong (A): A company''s own reacquired shares do not meet the definition of an asset. They represent a return of capital to selling shareholders and reduce equity, not increase assets.
Wrong (C): Treasury shares are not investments. They are the company''s own stock held in treasury, classified as a contra equity account rather than a noncurrent asset.
Wrong (D): Additional paid-in capital arises from stock issuances above par value. Treasury stock is a separate contra equity item, not a component of APIC.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11585;

-- Q11586: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 205-20-45-3, results of discontinued operations are reported net of tax as a separate component below income from continuing operations. Both the operating loss and disposal gain are presented within the discontinued operations section.
Wrong (A): Discontinued operations must be segregated from continuing operations to enable users to assess ongoing earnings quality. Combining them within operating expenses is prohibited.
Wrong (B): Other comprehensive income includes items like unrealized gains on AFS securities and foreign currency adjustments. Discontinued operations results are not OCI items.
