  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 230-10-45-12, proceeds from the sale of long-term assets such as equipment are classified as investing activities. The full $175,000 cash received is reported as an investing inflow. The $30,000 loss is a noncash reconciling item under the indirect method.
Wrong (A): Proceeds from selling equipment are investing activities, not operating activities. Operating activities involve revenue and expense-related cash flows from the entity''s central operations.
Wrong (B): Equipment disposals are not financing activities. Financing activities involve transactions with owners and creditors, not the sale of productive assets.
Wrong (C): The cash flow statement reports actual cash received ($175,000), not the net book value or a gain/loss-adjusted amount. The $30,000 loss does not reduce the reported cash inflow.$EXPL$
