-- Q11589: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 230-10-45-14 and 230-10-45-15, both transactions with creditors (issuing bonds) and transactions with owners (repurchasing stock) are classified as financing activities. The bond issuance is a $5 million financing inflow, and the stock repurchase is a $1.2 million financing outflow.
Wrong (A): Borrowing from creditors is a financing activity, not an investing activity. Returning capital to shareholders is also financing, not an operating activity.
Wrong (B): Bond issuance is a financing inflow, not an operating inflow. Operating activities relate to the entity''s revenue-generating transactions.
Wrong (D): Stock repurchase is a financing outflow, not an investing activity. Investing activities involve acquisitions and disposals of long-term assets and investments.$EXPL$
