-- Q11590: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 220-10-45, accumulated other comprehensive income is reported as a separate component of stockholders'' equity on the balance sheet. AOCI represents the cumulative total of items that bypassed net income but affected equity, such as unrealized losses on AFS securities.
Wrong (A): AOCI is not an asset. It is an equity adjustment reflecting cumulative OCI items, not a resource controlled by the entity.
Wrong (B): AOCI is not a liability. It represents accumulated equity adjustments, not obligations to transfer economic benefits.
Wrong (D): Other revenues and gains appear on the income statement. AOCI items bypass the income statement entirely and are reported directly in the equity section of the balance sheet.$EXPL$
